{"sections":[],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/tries"]}],"abstract":[{"text":"Tries over sequences of any ","type":"text"},{"code":"Hashable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" symbols, with prefix queries.","type":"text"}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Framework","externalID":"Tries","symbolKind":"module","modules":[{"name":"Tries"}],"role":"collection","title":"Tries"},"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/Trie","doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTree"],"anchor":"Sets-of-sequences","title":"Sets of sequences"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/TrieDictionary","doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTreeDictionary"],"anchor":"Dictionaries-keyed-by-sequences","title":"Dictionaries keyed by sequences"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/Trees"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Extended-Modules","title":"Extended Modules"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/Trie","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is a set of sequences and a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/TrieDictionary","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" a dictionary keyed by them, both kept in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a trie (Fredkin, 1960): a tree whose edges carry symbols and whose root-to-vertex paths spell the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"keys. They answer the queries a hash set cannot: every key with a prefix"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"elements(withPrefix:)"},{"type":"text","text":", whose "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"count"},{"type":"text","text":" is O(1)), whether any key has one ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"hasPrefix(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":"), and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the longest key that is a prefix of a query ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"longestPrefix(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["import Tries","","let words = Trie([\"car\", \"cart\", \"cat\", \"dog\"])","words.contains(\"cat\")                                   \/\/ true","words.elements(withPrefix: \"car\").map { String($0) }    \/\/ [\"car\", \"cart\"]","words.longestPrefix(of: \"carton\").map { String($0) }    \/\/ \"cart\""],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keys are any sequence of the symbol type and are stored as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[Symbol]"},{"type":"text","text":". For text, the symbol"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"type decides what a step is: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Trie<Character>"},{"type":"text","text":" steps by grapheme cluster, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Trie<Unicode.Scalar>"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"by scalar, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Trie<UInt8>"},{"type":"text","text":" over "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"utf8"},{"type":"text","text":" by byte, the fastest of the three, because comparing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"bytes is cheaper than comparing "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Character"},{"type":"text","text":"s. When the symbols are "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Comparable"},{"type":"text","text":", each vertex keeps"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its children sorted, so iteration is in lexicographic order; otherwise children come in the order"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"they were added."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTree","isActive":true},{"text":" and a ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTreeDictionary","isActive":true},{"text":" hold the same keys and answer the same queries,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with the same names, in a radix tree (Morrison, 1968): every chain of vertices with one child and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"no key is merged into one edge labelled with all its symbols, so there is a vertex per key and per","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"branching point rather than per symbol. They suit keys with long shared prefixes, such as file","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"paths or URLs, and build faster and in less memory than a trie of the same keys.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A trie’s shape converts to Grafluent’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PrefixTree"},{"text":" with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PrefixTree(_:)"},{"text":", and a radix tree’s to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Arborescence"},{"text":" of its vertices’ prefixes with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Arborescence(_:)"},{"text":" (import Grafluent’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Trees"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"module beside this one).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"references":{"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries":{"role":"collection","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Tries over sequences of any "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hashable"},{"type":"text","text":" symbols, with prefix queries."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries","url":"\/documentation\/tries","type":"topic","title":"Tries"},"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries/RadixTree":{"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A set of sequences kept in a radix tree (Morrison, 1968): a trie in which every chain of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertices with one child and no key is merged into one edge labelled with all its symbols."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTree","url":"\/documentation\/tries\/radixtree","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"RadixTree","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"RadixTree","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"RadixTree"},"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries/Trees":{"kind":"symbol","title":"Trees","role":"collection","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/tries\/trees","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/Trees","type":"topic"},"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries/Trie":{"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A set of sequences kept in a trie: a tree whose edges carry symbols and whose root-to-vertex"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"paths spell the keys (Fredkin, 1960)."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/Trie","url":"\/documentation\/tries\/trie","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Trie"}],"type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Trie"}],"title":"Trie"},"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries/RadixTreeDictionary":{"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A dictionary keyed by sequences, kept in a radix tree (Morrison, 1968): a trie in which every","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"chain of vertices with one child and no key is merged into one edge labelled with all its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"symbols, each key’s vertex holding its value.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTreeDictionary","url":"\/documentation\/tries\/radixtreedictionary","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"RadixTreeDictionary"}],"type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"RadixTreeDictionary"}],"title":"RadixTreeDictionary"},"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries/TrieDictionary":{"url":"\/documentation\/tries\/triedictionary","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A dictionary keyed by sequences, kept in a trie: a tree whose edges carry symbols and whose"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"root-to-vertex paths spell the keys, each key’s vertex holding its value (Fredkin, 1960)."}],"title":"TrieDictionary","type":"topic","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"TrieDictionary","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/TrieDictionary","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"TrieDictionary","kind":"identifier"}]}}}